==============================================================================
IBM Plex, the desktop app's lettering
==============================================================================

The desktop app (aptbim) letters its windows in two fonts that are built into its executable (crates/ui-egui/src/style.rs
includes them when it is compiled). They are kept in assets/fonts of the source:

  IBM Plex Sans, the variable font, Version 3.201
    assets/fonts/ibm-plex-sans/IBMPlexSans-Variable.ttf, 537244 bytes
    sha256 3b031aa4216174205bd8471f88a49b91f093169e9e87bd5262242bc5967fe2e3
    its name table says: Copyright 2019 IBM Corp. All rights reserved.

  IBM Plex Mono Regular, Version 2.3
    assets/fonts/ibm-plex-mono/IBMPlexMono-Regular.ttf, 135580 bytes
    sha256 6a3412f058c7d8dfd9170c41e85ade48e5156ecb89356110ca57a0a27734af46
    its name table says: Copyright 2017 IBM Corp. All rights reserved.

The notice that heads the licence file beside each of them reads:

    Copyright (c) 2017 IBM Corp. with Reserved Font Name "Plex"

These Font Software files are licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. Its text is in
assets/fonts/ibm-plex-sans/OFL.txt and assets/fonts/ibm-plex-mono/OFL.txt (the same text, one beside each font), and every
copy of AptBIM carries it: in a package the two files are fonts/ibm-plex-sans/OFL.txt and fonts/ibm-plex-mono/OFL.txt
beside this file (in the Linux packages under /usr/share/doc/aptbim, in the macOS app in Contents/Resources).

AptBIM does not change the fonts: it picks a weight of the variable font when it draws, and that is all. "Plex" is a
Reserved Font Name, so the fonts keep it. "IBM Plex" is a trademark of IBM Corp, registered in many jurisdictions worldwide.
The place the two files were obtained from was not recorded when they were added.
